I am quite pleased with this one. It's my first vegan ascension (having
been close but failed on a couple of previous attempts) and, while I've
done the other conducts before, I've certainly never had so many
conducts together previously.

I set out intending to do vegan, weaponless, artiwishless, and hopefully
get the polyless ones too. That would be 6 conducts, which would have
tied with the then-leading best behaved game on devnull. I got Magicbane
early, though, which gave me a source of MR, and I was lucky to get all
the amulets and rings I needed in the course of exploration, so I was
able to go wishless; and, with MB, I did genoless instead of weaponless.

That took me to 7 conducts, which is certainly a personal best and gave
me the lead of the best-behaved contest... for 2 hours, anyway, until
Tenaya's pacifist game equalled it.

Story of the game: (or skip to the end for the dumplog)

St:18/02 Dx:12 Co:11 In:9 - well, the Con is rather low, and I won't be
doing much casting. A useful general store on dlvl 2 provides jumping
boots (which I only used until finding some unidentified boots on dlvl
3) and a towel (useful for a vegetarian monk who won't get telepathy to
defend against lights).

There are altars on dlvl 3 and 4, both co-aligned. Just after finding
the second, a swarm of killer bees shows up, making an easy pile of
sacrifices. I don't hang around at altars prior to sokoban, but I will
sacrifice anything passing, so my pets and I kill them off and they go
on the altar - and I am gifted Magicbane.

Immediate MR is tempting, and although, practically speaking, that means
I'm abandoning weaponless, I can now do genoless instead (I tend to do
genoless when I have Magicbane, and have never done it without - the
curse resistance makes liches much less hassle). Also I'm much more
likely to succeed at genoless than weaponless (which is easy to
accidentally break), and having MR now makes polyselfless easy too; so I
calculate that I'll be making at least the same number of conducts as I
would and so would still match the current best behaved game of 6
conducts (all going well). So I switch to Magicbane for my main weapon
for the rest of the game.

I manage to haul enough corpses to the altar just from monsters turning
up in the next 50 turns to clear my prayer timeout, so the gift has not
endangered me when I go lower; and, unusually for me, I establish my
stash by the altar here (instead of in soko), as there is a large box
next to it and the downstairs are in the same room.

The level below is the Oracle, and I drag up equipment from a load of
Uruk-hai that I meet there to the altar to BUC-test: I get a +1 orcish
shield and +1 orcish helm, for AC 0. I also get gifted Frost Brand by
dragging up some rothe corpses [but I only use it against one brown mold
in the whole game, IIRC]. On the downside, my robe is now burned due to
stumbling into a magic trap and getting the pillar of fire effect.

I reach sokoban at turn 3200. I recruit a new kitten there, to give me a
pet to fight the soko zoo with (which I always do these days if I can,
as it seems to make fighting the zoo much safer). I get my unicorn horn
on the third level of soko. Unfortunately I get the bag of holding
sokoban, so I'm still short of reflection before the game can be
considered safe. The zoo is no problem, with AC -1 now and Magicbane,
and I have the gold and the BoH by turn 5800.

I head back to my stash, to BUC-test more loot. Some +2 iron shoes from
the zoo takes me to AC -3. And I have a ring of invisibility and a wand
of polymorph (which I stash as I'm hoping to go polyitemless). I have a
few potions of water and some junk potions which I now wipe, get my holy
water and bless my BoH. In identifying my potions I also reveal the
location of a vault on this level, and, since I'm not far from having
enough gold for one round of protection at minetown, I go back to
sokoban to retrieve a broad pick that I saw there so I can dig it out.

I made a rather beginner mistake at this point and wielded the mattock
to dig a more direct route across the Oracle level, only to find it was
cursed. Cursed 2-h weapon and I recently prayed for holy water... hmm.
On my way back to the stash, I encountered a F, which I kill and
sacrifice to check my prayer status; I could pray, so I did, solving
that problem.

I have a lantern from a shop, so I get to minetown without problem. +4
protection from the minetown priest makes me look a lot more
comfortable. I get the college-town minetown, with the spellbook shop
and tool, light, general, food shops; although I don't get much of use
from them. Heading down to mines' end, I have a bit of glitch when I
fall through a trap door to the level below mines' end that occurs in
devnull (related to one of the challenges, I assume, despite that I was
opted out of all challenges), which I don't realise until the upstairs
takes me into the mimic mines' end.

Mines' end provides the most dangerous moment, perhaps, prior to Kaen -
I walk round a corner into a mountain centaur with a wand of lightning.
Fortunately the bounce doesn't hit me as well. If I was playing smarter,
I would have zapped him with sleep next (my starting spell), but instead
I back around a corner, heal until he arrives, and hit him with
magicbane. I finish him with a zap of my wand of fire and the duel is
won (at the cost of just one vapourised ring from 3 hits of the wand).

I price-ID everything I can at minetown, buy all the spellbooks and
potions that I can afford, and head back to my stash. I'm in particular
price-IDing potions, so I can flag any potions with the same price as
polymorph and test the rest in the usual way. On the way back I get a
HoOA death-dropped by an orc, which I stash. At my stash, I bless and
read one of my L2-L3 spellbooks, hoping for identify or drain life
(already worried about Kaen), but I get the most useless spell in the
game, restore ability, instead; I'll continue to bless spellbooks and
read them as I can spare the water (int 9 is too low to safely read
anything without blessing).

I went back into sokoban next, to toss gems at a coaligned unicorn there
(identifying gems from glass and boosting my luck). I then started
exploring down towards the castle. I got the bigroom, and it was a bones
level too, of "bhaak, killed by a tiger". It was a valkyrie bones, with
Mjollnir (didn't use), an amulet (which I hoped would be reflection, but
was actually ESP), the usual +3 small shield (which became my shield for
the rest of the game), a cloak of magic resistance [as I found later,
but which I only used for convenience during the ascension run], speed
boots and some scrolls. I price-IDed the scrolls, but the only 80zm
scroll I had proved to be enchant armor, so I wiped more potions to
water and just dipped individual items that I needed in holy water to
uncurse them. I get an amulet of reflection a few levels further down,
though, and so I now have MR, reflection, SR, PR, unihorn and should be
safe to ascend.

I was starting to think of doing wishless in addition to my intended
conducts, so by this point I was scouring the dungeon more thoroughly
that I normally would - in particular digging up every grave and
breaking every statue. I got lucky with one of these and got a pair of
lenses, very handy for a caster with In: 9 - enough that I could read L1
spells with only a small amount of danger (albeit it was the
higher-level spellbooks I really wanted to be able to read). I was
clearing every lep hall as well, building up gold to buy more
protection; after getting enough gold for 3 rounds of protection, I went
back to minetown to get it, taking me to AC -11. On the way I price-IDed
more loot (there being no general store below dlvl 4), and empty my
stash (aiming to establish my main stash at the castle). I pray for more
holy water (I'm worried about running out, due to seeing no scrolls of
remove curse yet) and I get crowned, which isn't very useful but does
give me Vorpal (to shove it a trunk, out of the way for Astral).

I get down to Medusa, and it's the Titan Medusa, so I back out
immediately and take stock. I return to fountains on an earlier level to
wipe potions for more holy water (including wiping some healing potions,
which I regret later on). I offload more gold to the nearest priest,
managing to get to 10 points of divine protection for AC -15. Good for a
mid-game monk, but I'll be relying on my sleep spell to keep minotaurs
at bay.

I head down to fight the titan, who immediately summons the usual
selection of master mind flayer, black dragon, jabberwock and Elvenking.
Elbereth scares most of them off and I think I'm doing well, until the
titan drinks a potion of full healing and backs out of melee range (I
have no ranged attacks to speak of - just unskilled darts). Someone
throws a boulder which blocks line of sight to the titan and I'm able to
clear the first wave of summons with the black dragon's help. Once the
titan is back in sight, I get another elf lord (this time with an amulet
of life saving, just to be annoying), disenchanter, another dragon, and
the usual mixture of other enemies. The titan eventually strays too
close once too often and I have won, without being in too much danger at
any point.

I get across Medusa and the castle is the level below - and I realise I
have no instrument. I saw one ages ago, but will have to trek back for
it;  unfortunately I have a food problem too, since I'm down to one food
ration, partly due to casting 'light' a lot (but I have divination at
basic as a result, and one of my spellbooks is found to be magic
mapping). I have to dump my spellbooks at the castle entrance, and run
all the way back to my old stash at the top of the dungeon just to pick
up my last 2 spare food rations and grab the instrument on the way.

Back at the castle, I use the drawbridge to kill the liches, nagas and
undead, and let everything else across - I need all the loot I can get.
Halfway through, but after the liches and nagas are dead, a soldier
blows up the drawbridge, so I do the usual scroll of earth to bridge the
moat. I soon clear out the throne room and barracks, getting to xl14 at
the same time; I have the wand of wishing [0:2] by turn 20600. I clear
the Valley next, hoping for more equipment (particularly for a spellbook
of drain life), but get just the usual scroll and potion fodder. I have
a couple of potions of gain ability by now, though, which I bless and
drink, so I have Int 11 and lenses and so can read most of my spellbooks
at last; I now have identify, and also remove curse (the spell) (a poor
substitute for scrolls, but better than nothing).

Time to go and face Kaen. On the way, I use up all my wands of create
monster sacrificing at an altar - so I can pray for more holy water (I'm
still worried about running out so even saving one potion by praying
instead of dipping). My main hope, though, is that I'll get a marker or
useful scrolls on the death drops; instead, the most useful items I get
are a couple of extra healing potions. I use my available scrolls of
enchant armour to get Magicbane to +7.

I clear down to Kaen's level with no problem, and get a scroll of remove
curse along the way, which eases my mind a bit. But still no magic
marker, so I have only a limited ability to enchant my armour; I get to
AC -22 with the scrolls that I have. I alchemise up some full healing
potions, but even so I only have 5, so I drink a couple to boost my
hitpoints and keep some out as I'm afraid I'll need them. I'm clearly
too weak to try any kind of fight with Kaen, so I'll try to put him to
sleep and use a boulder fort as soon as he starts hitting me. I do need
the boulder fort, and finally a shot of sleep immobilises him; I then
zap him with a wands of cold and lightning from inside the fort until he
croaks.

Into Gehennom next. There is a demilich at Asmodeus', which summons a
lot of stuff but causes no particular problem to beat. With magic
mapping at around 50%, I have no problems mapping my way down. I'm
carrying a potion of acid around in my inventory now, in case I get hit
by a 'trice (lizard corpse breaks vegan, of course). I find a magic
marker around the same time, my first of the game, which is the only
thing I lacked. Orcus' town is easily cleared by a 'trice corpse; I do
my final preparations here, with another two potions of gain ability
taking me to Int 13, and enchanting my armour so I have AC -27. I have
only 134 hitpoints, which is low for me, hence wanting the good AC. I
then have to chase down a master lich at the VS level, and it takes a
while to pin him down at the upstairs on the level above and then clear
all the summoned enemies (including 3 minotaurs - lots of shots of sleep
required). I have found the VS by turn 27000.

I get a 'trice corpse outside the Wizard's tower, which clears the
liches in the tower, the Wizard himself, and the liches in the Sanctum -
I have a ring of teleport control and enough cursed scrolls of teleport
to levelport straight to the top of the tower, then straight to the VS,
and then straight into the sanctum. There is rather a large fight in the
sanctum, with a demilich and a nalfeeshee summoning enemies; and I
zapped a wand of sleep for illumination, which encouraged all the
priests to summon insects at a distance. I end up killing most of the
priests with the 'trice corpse just to get some peace, and finally kill
the High Priest with it too. I get out of the sanctum by cursing my only
remaining potion of gain level.

The ascent goes poorly; the mysterious force compels me to cross
Juiblex's swamp 9 times. On one of those, a master lich gets randomely
summoned, and summons a lot of enemies on the level above, which is a
hassle to clear up. As I have plenty of wands of death, and have left
lots of 'trices in the main dungeon, I have plenty of ways to kill the
Wizard when he shows up; I'm feeling confident so I don't bother
collecting my HoOA (I've never yet used one for Astral). I still have a
'trice corpse when I start the planes, which comes in handy for the
Wizard on Earth and for the arch-lich that gets summoned on Air.
Unfortunately the corpse has rotted away by the time I reach Fire, and
there's an Archon between me and the portal; I'm forced to burn E
multiple times (very glad of the Eyes to let me do that) and teleport
him out of the way.

I clear the purple Ls on Astral, then head for the rightmost sanctum
without looking first (I'm too scared to switch to my amulet of ESP just
to get a quick blindfold look at who's who, which is what I was doing
while exploring the dungeon). Unfortunately this sanctum turns out to be
Death's, and I have no good ranged attacks. I jump past him on the way
in; but it's the wrong altar, and I have trouble avoiding Death on the
way out; I use one potion of full healing here while clearing out the
angels and priest (aided by conflict), then lead Death in a circle
around the back of the temple to leave him behind.

The centre sanctum is crowded and hard to get through, although I jump
past Pesty okay. It's the wrong altar again. I kill Pesty with a wand of
death a couple of times getting through, but with the help of conflict,
and using my marker to write charging for my teleport wands, I get
out. Wand of death takes out Famine in the final sanctum, and I'm easily
through to the right altar at last.




